message: "If you use this Implementation Guide, please cite the published article (preferred-citation) and, if you need to reference the artefacts themselves, this repository at the release you used."
type: software
title: "iOS Lifestyle Medicine FHIR Implementation Guide"
abstract: "HL7 FHIR R4 Implementation Guide for consumer-wearable lifestyle-medicine data (heart-rate variability, SpO2, sleep, physical activity, nutrition, stress, social and environmental determinants) with openEHR and OMOP ConceptMaps, a verified terminology ledger, and CDS Hooks / SMART on FHIR / Bulk Data conformance resources."
